  "adaptations": [
    "Existing native collections, selection manager, View refs, coordinates and owned transfer resources replace DOM types; no react-aria runtime dependency.",
    "Draggable/droppable state algorithms retain source key selection, ancestor filtering, drag callbacks and drop target/operation behavior.",
    "Private source only; native action handoff, OS transfer, Table/Sort integration and all source/consumer/product/native gates remain required.",
    "Private retirement clears owned refs/state without invoking stale end/exit handlers.",
    "Physical lift preserves onDragStart/getItems/representation-write/allowed-operation order. Preview items retain original JS identity; virtual mode does not eagerly read representation getters.",
    "Native list targeting consumes original root/item geometry cohorts and retains typed keys; it returns no item target for an unmaterialized native row.",
    "OS data drivers, native action handoff, custom preview/keyboard/AT adapters, complete hook factory and Table/Sort bindings remain unimplemented in this core increment; no public export follows."
  ]
}
